course: dictionary
lesson: 9957
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it, because they are the context. «The Māori are famous for carving and tattooing.» Carving is an art, so tattooing here means making art on the skin.
explain: A tattoo is a picture or pattern made on the skin with ink, pushed in by a needle, and it stays there. Tattoo can also be a verb: you tattoo a design onto someone's skin. Check the grammar too: a tattoo is a thing, and tattooing is an action.
explain: Tattoo has two other meanings. A military tattoo is a show with music, marching and drums, often at night. A tattoo can also be a steady beating or tapping sound, like rain drumming on a window. Ask: which meaning fits? Swap it into the sentence and check.
fact: A tattoo is a picture or pattern made on the skin with ink pushed in by a needle.
fact: «Tattoo» can be a noun (a tattoo, tattoos) or a verb (tattoo, tattooed, tattooing).
fact: Many adults have tattoos, and in many places you must be an adult to get one.
fact: A «military tattoo» is a festival show with music, marching and drums, often at night.
fact: «Tā moko» is a traditional Māori form of tattooing in New Zealand, and it has deep meanings in that culture.
exercise: «The Māori are famous for carving, tattooing and the haka.» What does tattooing mean here? | Playing loud drums at night | Marching in a show | Beating like rain on a window | *Making pictures on the skin with ink and a needle
exercise: The steady tattoo of rain on the tent kept Ella awake. What does tattoo mean? | A picture on the skin | A show with marching bands | A kind of tent | *A steady tapping sound
exercise: Which word completes the sentence? The artist ___ a dragon onto his arm last year. | tattooing | tattoos | *tattooed | tattoo
test: «The crowd cheered as the soldiers marched past at the military tattoo.» Which meaning fits tattoo here? | *A show with music, marching and drums | To draw on skin | A picture made with a needle | A tapping sound like rain
test: Which word is a verb in «She wants to tattoo a bird on her wrist»? | *tattoo | wrist | to | bird
exam: The crowd cheered as the soldiers marched past at the military tattoo. What does tattoo mean? | To make a design on skin | A steady tapping sound | *A show with music, marching and drums | A picture made with a needle
